Z||000000||Formula||05-25-2000||09:38 PM||||I went to cars.com and looked up the stats on a 1990 Mustang GT........<P>225 hp<BR>300 ft. lbs<BR>2824 lbs..........How in the he!! is a 5.0 close to the same weight as a fiero GT????<BR>My Formula weighs around 2700.......<BR>Whats up with this.  <BR>The 4 cyl stangs weigh in at 2759 lbs.<BR>This is just wrong.<P>I always thought they weighed a good 3500 lbs.  Welp, there goes our "huge" weight advantage.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||05-26-2000||04:13 AM||||The GVW for my 92 Mustang GT Convertible is 3200lbs. Now take out the driver, payload and full tank of gas. 2700lbs is about right||||reg||10
Z||000002||fierospeeder||05-26-2000||04:21 AM||||my 87 tbird turbo weighs somewhere around 3500lbs.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||sid1200||05-26-2000||05:12 AM||||79-93 V8 Mustangs are known to be light.<P>Also known to have god awful brakes , but light nonetheless.<P>the 94+ gained about 250-300 lbs.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||05-26-2000||06:40 AM||||Our cars are deceptively heavy. Mine weighs 3068 with me in it and 1/2 tank of gas.||||reg||1
Z||000005||2birds||05-26-2000||11:34 PM||||Why do you suppose they were so popular?  Lighter, cheaper, more moddable than anything else built in the late 80's/early 90's.  They were the king of the street until the LT1 F-body came out, and Ford still sells every one they make.  Supposedly a new Z-28 is cheaper and faster than a Mustang GT, but if you can FIND a Z, it'll be so loaded out and slushboxed that it costs more than the Mustang.  Saw a new Z-28 SS convertible today, $34,850.  Cobra convertible, $32,500.  And there are 10 times the Mustang GT's as Z-28/Trans Am/Formula's on the used car market, too.||||reg||1
Z||000006||BBBAD GT||05-27-2000||01:22 AM||||I seriously doubt a stock 86-93 5.0 would come in below 3k without driver.  Sure, there are a ton of things you can do to lighten them up, but 2.7k without driver is totally unrealistic IMO.  I weigh my 89 5.0 everytime I'm at the track, and it hovers around 3.4k (me in it, 160lb)with the following weight mods (approx):<P>Glass Hood -20lb<BR>Remove AC -20lb<BR>Rollbar +90lb<BR>Scat shield +40lb<BR>TKO 5sp +70lb<BR>Delete spare -20lb<BR>Delete backseat -10lb<BR>Subframes +30lb<BR>Blower +70lb<P>Add it up, and you get close to 3.2k when stock, which I think is avg (hatch or noch).<P><BR>||||reg||1
